WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.300
Deputy. A deputy is an agreed stand-in who carries out specified duties for someone else during an agreed period. In this case, Aisha may cover Daniel’s work only after she has accepted the particular duties and dates and has the information and access she needs. Being named as deputy does not give her all of Daniel’s responsibilities or unlimited decision authority. Any limits and unresolved arrangements must remain clear.
